text:
maria: heads up — saw a burst of 429s from eu-west app traffic right after the nightly model swap. looks like pool fill + a handful of long-running prompts causing long queue tails. anyone seeing similar traces?

sunil: yep, tracing shows 3 GPUs in pool hit 95% memory and stayed pinned. a subset of requests held KV cache for +8s which blocked batching.

benjamin: interesting — admission control dropped to 0.5s admit window and clients started getting 429s with Retry-After=2. some clients retried aggressively and amplified the pressure.

katie: can we add a lightweight header so SDKs can make smarter decisions? current Retry-After is too binary.

maria: proposing we emit a small hint set on 429s and 200s:
```
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 2
X-RW-Admit-Window-Ms: 150    # how long admission window is open
X-RW-Pool-Fill-Pct: 92       # approximate pool GPU fill percent
X-RW-Queue-Estimate-Ms: 3200 # rough median wait for current queue
X-RW-Fallback-Region: eu-central # optional suggestion for geo-fallback
```

sunil: love the idea. Queue-Estimate-Ms is approximate but useful for client pacing vs full retry.

yousef: SDK behavior I'd recommend: on 429 with these headers, do: 1) if Queue-Estimate-Ms < 5000 then jittered backoff with cap 3 retries; 2) if Pool-Fill-Pct > 90 and Queue-Estimate-Ms > 2000 then route to fallback-region if present; 3) exponential base 100ms with full-jitter, max backoff 5s.

benjamin: also add a per-route concurrency header so clients can limit parallelism at source: X-RW-Allowed-Concurrency: 8

katie: small patch for SDK pseudocode:
```js
const base = 100; // ms
const jitter = () => Math.random() * base;
async function handle429(resp) {
  const q = Number(resp.headers.get('X-RW-Queue-Estimate-Ms') || 0);
  const pool = Number(resp.headers.get('X-RW-Pool-Fill-Pct') || 0);
  const allowed = Number(resp.headers.get('X-RW-Allowed-Concurrency') || 4);
  if (pool > 90 && q > 2000 && resp.headers.get('X-RW-Fallback-Region')) {
    return routeTo(resp.headers.get('X-RW-Fallback-Region'));
  }
  // jittered exponential with caps
  let attempt = 0;
  while(attempt < 3) {
    await sleep((Math.pow(2, attempt) * base) + jitter());
    attempt++;
    // send again with awareness of allowed concurrency
  }
}
```

yousef: quick ops detail — exposing Pool-Fill-Pct is low risk but helps client-side load-shedding and cuts cost spikes from retry storms. We should cap precision to avoid exact capacity leakage (round to nearest 5%).

maria: ops-bot posted scaling events when pool switched to reduced capacity during maintenance; that combined with the long prompts created the fat tail. ops-bot: "reduced-capacity mode enabled for eu-west pool at 1865431800"

ops-bot: reduced-capacity mode enabled for eu-west pool at 1865431800 (expected duration 15m).

benjamin: follow-up: we should also emit a short-lived admission token TTL header so SDKs can pre-check admission windows without full request: X-RW-Admit-TTL-Sec

katie: agree. then client can do a light HEAD to probe with tiny footprint.

maria: action items: 1) eng-ml to add header prototypes on canary (sunil, benjamin) 2) SDK team to implement jitter/backoff + fallback-region logic (katie, yousef) 3) oncall to add a dashboard showing queue-estimate distribution (maria)

sunil: starting branch now, will post diff link when ready.

